                "text": "I'm mapping the input grid's border lines (9, 7, 2, 8) to figure out the output dimensions of 9x8, then working through how the interior rows and columns correspond between input and output, counting 8s per row to determine the pattern.\n\nNow I'm noticing the counts don't line up cleanly with a simple row-count theory, so I'm reconsidering whether the relevant region spans different rows or columns, possibly including the 8-line and 9-line as border columns in the output itself since column0 is all 8s and column7 is all 9s.\n\nTesting the region rows3-11, cols3-10 directly against the actual grid values, rows 3-5 match the output rows perfectly, but row6 breaks the pattern\u2014so I'm suspecting the 8s inside a row might trigger a fill from the border column up to that 8's position, like a partial line being drawn toward it.\n\nand 2 lines, with the quadrant between them containing scattered 8s that get connected back to the 8 line. I feel confident enough in this rule to test it now.",
